{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"203","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Game on Paper"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One not particularly beautiful evening Valera got very bored. To amuse himself a little bit, he found the following game."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He took a checkered white square piece of paper, consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cells. After that, he started to paint the white cells black one after the other. In total he painted "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" different cells on the piece of paper. Since Valera was keen on everything square, he wondered, how many moves (i.e. times the boy paints a square black) he should make till a black square with side "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be found on the piece of paper. But Valera does not know the answer to this question, so he asks you to help him."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to find the minimum number of moves, till the checkered piece of paper has at least one black square with side of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":". Otherwise determine that such move does not exist."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ m ≤ min(n·n, 105))"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the size of the squared piece of paper and the number of moves, correspondingly. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the description of the moves. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ xi, yi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of row and column of the square that gets painted on the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th move. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"All numbers on the lines are separated by single spaces. It is guaranteed that all moves are different. The moves are numbered starting from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the order, in which they are given in the input. The columns of the squared piece of paper are numbered starting from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", from the left to the right. The rows of the squared piece of paper are numbered starting from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", from top to bottom."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On a single line print the answer to the problem — the minimum number of the move after which the piece of paper has a black square with side "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":". If no such move exists, print -1."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 11\n1 1\n1 2\n1 3\n2 2\n2 3\n1 4\n2 4\n3 4\n3 2\n3 3\n4 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 12\n1 1\n1 2\n1 3\n2 2\n2 3\n1 4\n2 4\n3 4\n3 2\n4 2\n4 1\n3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"203B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/203/problem/B"}